Git source steps no longer print URL userinfo in the commands they log, except for a bare username on an ``ssh://`` URL, where Git's URL syntax is ``ssh://[<user>@]<host>`` with no password field and the username is not a secret. The worker still receives the real URL, so this does not remove credentials from worker process arguments or from an ordinary checkout's ``remote.origin.url``, and it does not attempt to identify secrets passed as URL query parameters. Obfuscation applies to workers connected over the default protocol; on the experimental msgpack protocol the real URL is logged as before. Use ``auth_credentials`` or ``git_credentials`` to keep secrets out of ``repourl`` entirely.
